<title>PORTUGAL: Portugal March retail sales index up 13.9 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Portugal March retail sales index up 13.9 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-07-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Portugal's March retail sales index rose 13.9 percent to 153.4 from February and up 5.3 percent from a year ago, the National Statistics Institute (INE) said.</p>
<p>INE gave the following figures for retail sales:</p>
<p>					Mar		Feb	   Mar '96</p>
<p>    Index (base 1990)	   153.4	    134.7	  145.6</p>
<p>Components:</p>
<p>    Food and drink		183.3	    153.6	  183.2</p>
<p>    Chemical/pharmaceutical   181.1	    183.3	  170.3</p>
<p>    Clothing/footwear/textile 202.3	    181.0	  181.4</p>
<p>    Furniture		     120.8	    104.7	  104.2</p>
<p>    Construction materials    137.5	    124.6	  122.8</p>
<p>    Vehicles			125.0	    110.1	  109.8</p>
<p>    Fuel			    149.9	    142.4	  153.0</p>
<p>    Warehouse/market sales    126.4	    105.4	  129.7</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +(351-1) 3538254</p>
</text>
